tip: | Look at the dog. | Sitting is the easiest pose to read: head up, chest forward, haunch low, tail on the ground.
tip: 1 | A silhouette, not an outline. | Snout, back, tail. You should know it is a dog from this one flat shape.
tip: 4 | The ear goes on last. | A floppy ear two steps darker sits inside the silhouette, so it has to wait for the details. That one patch says dog more than anything else.
tip: 3 | Fur is a ramp. | The light chest and muzzle are one step on the same ramp as the darker back. No new color, just a shift along it.
tip: | The other facing. | Animals face a way, so a flip gives you the second one for nothing. Most animals are close enough to symmetric that nobody notices.
